      "id": "bk2-vas-006",
      "q": "An 80-year-old with a hostile abdomen needs AAA repair while a fit 60-year-old also needs one. The EVAR lesson is?",
      "o": [
        "Open for every aneurysm",
        "Stents for every aneurysm",
        "No repair after eighty",
        "Stent graft for the frail, open repair for the young fit"
      ],
      "a": 3,
      "exp": "EVAR-1 gave early wins that converge late, so frail hostile abdomens take stents while young fit patients take durable open repair.",
      "r": [
        "Incorrect. Frail abdomens suit stents.",
        "Incorrect. Young fit last longer open.",
        "Incorrect. Age alone never decides.",
        "Correct. Fitness and age choose."
      ],
      "kp": "Frail takes EVAR, fit young takes open.",
      "source": "EVAR-1 trial with ESVS guidance",
      "topic": "sva-arterial"
